.TH ZEZA 1 "November 2026" "z/OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zeza \- Python eza clone tailored for z/OS UNIX System Services (USS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zeza
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATHS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zeza
is a feature-rich, modern file-listing utility inspired by \fBeza\fR, designed specifically for IBM z/OS. It provides robust colorized terminal output, native EBCDIC/ASCII tag support, extended attribute inspection, zFS dataset resolution, and Git status integration. 

It features both a standard CLI format and an interactive full-screen Text User Interface (TUI) for navigating, sorting, filtering, editing, and managing files directly on the mainframe.
.SH CLI OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a, \-\-all\fR
Show hidden files (starting with .).
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-long\fR
Display extended metadata (permissions, links, owner, group, size, time).
.TP
\fB\-g, \-\-git\fR
Show Git status badges and the current repository branch.
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-time\fR
Sort by modification time (newest first).
.TP
\fB\-i, \-\-icons\fR
Display Nerd Font icons next to filenames.
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-blocks\fR
Display file sizes in 512-byte blocks instead of standard bytes.
.TP
\fB\-J, \-\-json\fR \fIFILE\fR
Export directory listing data to a specified JSON file.
.TP
\fB\-e, \-\-ext\fR \fIEXT\fR
Filter by comma-separated file extensions (e.g., txt,rex,c).
.TP
\fB\-R, \-\-regex\fR \fIPATTERN\fR
Filter files matching a regular expression.
.TP
\fB\-T, \-\-tags\fR
Display z/OS file tags (state and codeset, via chtag).
.TP
\fB\-x, \-\-extattr\fR
Display z/OS extended attributes (APF, program control, shared address space, shared library).
.TP
\fB\-\-tree\fR
Display output in a recursive tree topology.
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-directory\fR
List directories themselves, not their contents.
.TP
\fB\-S, \-\-sort\-size\fR
Sort files by size (largest first).
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-reverse\fR
Reverse the current sort order.
.TP
\fB\-1, \-\-oneline\fR
Display one entry per line.
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-dsn\fR
Show underlying zFS dataset names for directories and symlinks. Caches mount points for performance.
.TP
\fB\-\-tui\fR
Launch the interactive fullscreen Text User Interface. Can be combined with shell globs (e.g., zeza --tui z*).
.SH TUI HOTKEYS
.TP
\fBNavigation\fR
UP/DOWN (Move cursor), ENTER (Open Directory/File), ESC (Go up one directory).
.TP
\fBFile Operations\fR
.B e
(Edit file),
.B D
(Delete),
.B R
(Rename),
.B C
(Copy).
.TP
\fBSorting & Filtering\fR
.B s
(Size),
.B t
(Time),
.B n
(Name),
.B r
(Reverse). Press
.B f
or
.B /
to filter by string, and
.B c
to clear the active filter.
.TP
\fBSystem\fR
.B o
(Open settings for colors/editor),
.B F1
(Show help tutorial),
.B q
(Quit).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.pyeza.json\fR
User configuration file storing TUI terminal color preferences and default editor commands.
.SH BUGS
z/OS DSFS reads can be slow. Use \fBCtrl+C\fR to abort hanging directory reads safely.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the z/OS community.
